// =============================================================================
// core/subtle/mod.vr — operations defined by what the machine must NOT do
// =============================================================================
// Layer: 0 (core primitives + intrinsics)
// =============================================================================
//

// Ordinary code is specified by the value it computes. The operations
// here are specified by what must NOT happen while computing it —
// which is why an obvious-looking rewrite silently destroys them.
//

//  * `constant_time` — comparison and selection whose timing does not
//    depend on secret data. `==` on two byte strings exits at the
//    first difference, so its running time reveals the length of the
//    correct prefix: enough to forge a MAC tag byte by byte. Used for
//    every tag, password-hash and token comparison.
//
//  * `zeroize`       — wipes that survive optimisation. A compiler may
//    delete a store to memory that is never read again, which is
//    exactly the shape of erasing a key before free. These wipes are
//    written so that they cannot be elided.
//

// The name follows the term of art (`crypto/subtle`) for this class:
// primitives whose misuse is invisible in the result and only shows up
// under measurement or attack.
//

// =============================================================================

module core.subtle;

public module constant_time;
public module zeroize;
